{"kind":{"type":"frontMatter","text":"title: \"ssh fetch logs in as the wrong GitHub account: agent key order and a dropped IdentitiesOnly\"\u000adate: 2026-09-29\u000acategory: integration-issues\u000amodule: rc-git-guard\u000aproblem_type: integration_issue\u000acomponent: infrastructure\u000asymptoms:\u000a  - \"fetch 'origin': An IO error occurred when talking to the server: failed to fill whole buffer\"\u000a  - \"rc-git fetch fails on an ssh-config alias remote while git ls-remote on the same repository succeeds\"\u000a  - \"ssh -T git@github.com greets a different account than the alias's IdentityFile key belongs to\"\u000a  - \"GitHub's 'Repository not found' goes to the channel's stderr, which rc-git never reads\"\u000aroot_cause: logic_error\u000aresolution_type: code_fix\u000aseverity: high\u000arelated_components:\u000a  - rc-git-core\u000atags: [ssh, russh, russh-config, identitiesonly, ssh-agent, github, openssh-parity, fetch]"},"runs":[],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":1},"runs":[{"text":"ssh fetch logs in as the wrong GitHub account: agent key order and a dropped IdentitiesOnly","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Problem","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"rc-git's in-process ssh transport offered keys in a different order from OpenSSH. On a multi-account alias remote (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"git@github.com-work:example-org/example-repo.git","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", whose ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"~/.ssh/config","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" block sets ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"HostName github.com","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentityFile <work key>","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentitiesOnly yes","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") it offered every ssh-agent key first, in agent order. GitHub accepted the first one, which belonged to a different account, and that account cannot see the repository. Every fetch and Sync on the remote failed with an error that looked like a network fault.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Symptoms","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"App Sync dialog: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rc-git could not sync — fetch 'origin': An IO error occurred when talking to the server","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"CLI, after about 3 s: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rc-git fetch <repo>","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" → ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"fetch 'origin': An IO error occurred when talking to the server: An IO error occurred when talking to the server: failed to fill whole buffer","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". This is not a lookup error or a timeout: the connection was made, authenticated, and then the stream ended.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"git ls-remote origin","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" on the same repository works, and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ssh -T git@github.com-work","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" greets the right account (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Hi <work-account>!","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":").","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"ssh -T git@github.com","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" greets a different account (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Hi <personal-account>!","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"), the owner of the first key in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ssh-add -l","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". The agent held five keys, and the one the alias names was third.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"What Didn't Work","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Treating it as host resolution.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" The earlier alias fix already resolves ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"HostName","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" through russh-config (see the related doc). The about-3-second failure and the EOF, with no lookup error, show that the dial reached GitHub and got through authentication.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Treating it as a transport or framing bug.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"failed to fill whole buffer","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is std's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"UnexpectedEof","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" message. It means gix's handshake asked for a pkt-line and the channel closed first. The real reason was on the channel's stderr, which rc-git did not read at the time: the transport wrapped russh's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"channel.into_stream()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", a reader over stdout only, so GitHub's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ERROR: Repository not found.","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" was dropped and gix reported the EOF instead. Since then ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"transport","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/actions/remote/ssh.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") splits the channel and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"SshRead","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" reads through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ChannelReader","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ssh/output.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"), which takes stdout, stderr and the exit status off one queue and ends the stream with a ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ServerRefusal","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" carrying the server's stderr.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Using ","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"git ls-remote","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" as the control.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" It proves the config and the key are good. OpenSSH orders keys correctly, though, so it cannot expose an ordering bug. What cracked it was checking which identity each path authenticates as: match the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ssh-add -l","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" fingerprints against ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ssh-keygen -lf <key>.pub","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", then compare ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ssh -T git@github.com","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (first agent key wins) with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ssh -T git@github.com-work","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (the configured key wins).","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A narrower fix would not have been enough.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" Honoring ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentitiesOnly","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" alone fixes this config but not the same alias without ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentitiesOnly","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". OpenSSH still offers the configured key before the agent's other keys there, while the old ladder would still lead with agent order.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Solution","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The fix makes the ladder follow OpenSSH's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"pubkey_prepare","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"sshconnect2.c","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"): first agent keys that match a configured identity file, in agent order; then the agent's other keys unless ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentitiesOnly","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"; then the identity files the agent does not hold, in config order. rc-git's agent read keeps only plain public keys (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"connect_agent","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" skips every ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"AgentIdentity","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" that is not ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"PublicKey","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"), so the certificate steps OpenSSH puts first do not arise. All three parts are in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/actions/remote/ssh/","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"1. Offer order","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"offer_order","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"auth.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). This is a pure function over comparable keys, so it is unit-tested with integers. An agent key that matches a file stands in for that file, so the file is not offered a second time:","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"code","language":"rust","text":"fn offer_order<K: PartialEq>(\u000a    agent: &[K],\u000a    files: &[Option<K>],\u000a    identities_only: bool,\u000a) -> Vec<Offer> {\u000a    let mut covered = vec![false; files.len()];\u000a    let mut matched = Vec::new();\u000a    let mut unmatched = Vec::new();\u000a    for (index, key) in agent.iter().enumerate() {\u000a        let mut matches_a_file = false;\u000a        for (file, file_key) in files.iter().enumerate() {\u000a            if file_key.as_ref() == Some(key) {\u000a                covered[file] = true;\u000a                matches_a_file = true;\u000a            }\u000a        }\u000a        if matches_a_file {\u000a            matched.push(Offer::Agent(index));\u000a        } else if !identities_only {\u000a            unmatched.push(Offer::Agent(index));\u000a        }\u000a    }\u000a    let mut order = matched;\u000a    order.extend(unmatched);\u000a    for (file, covered) in covered.into_iter().enumerate() {\u000a        if !covered {\u000a            order.push(Offer::File(file));\u000a        }\u000a    }\u000a    order\u000a}"},"runs":[],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"authenticate","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" calls it through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"key_order","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which compares keys by ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"key_identity","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" — ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"PublicKey::key_data()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" rather than ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"PublicKey","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". ssh-key derives ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"PartialEq","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" on ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"PublicKey","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" over the comment too (ssh-key 0.7.0-rc.11, ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"src/public.rs:94-106","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", a dependency path). The agent's copy and the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".pub","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" file's copy usually have different comments, so whole-key equality never matches. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"file_public_key","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" follows OpenSSH's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"sshkey_load_public","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" order: the file itself when ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentityFile","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" names a public key (it then stands only for the agent key it matches), then ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"<path>.pub","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", then the public half an OpenSSH-format private key stores in the clear, so an encrypted key matches its agent copy without a passphrase. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"authenticate","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" walks the order through a ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Ladder","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (handle, target, RSA hash, op). Each offer ends as an ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Outcome","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":": ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Accepted","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Rejected","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Locked","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (the passphrase, or its absence, cannot open the file), ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Unusable","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" with a reason, or ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Absent","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (a default identity file that does not exist). Only when nothing was accepted does ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ladder_error","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" pick the error: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"PassphraseRequired","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for the first locked file, else a ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Git","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" error naming each unusable file, else ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"AuthRequired","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"2. ","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentitiesOnly","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is read, although russh-config drops it.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" russh-config 0.58.0's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"HostConfig","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" has only ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"user","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"hostname","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"port","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"identity_file","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"proxy_command","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"proxy_jump","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"add_keys_to_agent","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"user_known_hosts_file","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"strict_host_key_checking","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"~/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/russh-config-0.58.0/src/lib.rs:30-49","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). Its parser sends any other key to a ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"debug!","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and throws it away (same file, ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"lib.rs:291-293","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). rc-git builds a second view of the normalized config that keeps only ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Host","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" lines and rewrites each line of one directive as ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"User <v>","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"directive_as_user","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"target.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", used today for ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentitiesOnly","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"HostKeyAlias","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentityAgent","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"):","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"code","language":"rust","text":"fn directive_as_user(normalized: &str, keyword: &str) -> String {\u000a    let mut view = String::new();\u000a    for line in normalized.lines() {\u000a        let line = line.trim_start();\u000a        let (key, value) = line.split_once(' ').unwrap_or((line, \"\"));\u000a        if key.eq_ignore_ascii_case(\"host\") {\u000a            view.push_str(line);\u000a        } else if key.eq_ignore_ascii_case(keyword) {\u000a            view.push_str(\"User \");\u000a            view.push_str(value);\u000a        } else {\u000a            continue;\u000a        }\u000a        view.push('\\n');\u000a    }\u000a    view\u000a}"},"runs":[],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"load_config","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" parses that view through the same ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"parse_for_host","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" as the real config and reads ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".user","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" as the directive's value; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentitiesOnly","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" counts as set for ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"yes","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" or ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"true","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", quoted or not. Only ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Host","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" lines survive in the view, so a real ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"User","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" directive cannot leak into the answer.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"3. Default keys only when no ","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentityFile","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" applies","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"resolve","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"target.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which sets ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"identities_configured","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). rc-git used to append ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"id_ed25519","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"id_ecdsa","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"id_rsa","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" after any configured files; it now falls back to OpenSSH's default list only when the config names none. OpenSSH adds them only when ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"num_identity_files == 0","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"fill_default_options","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"readconf.c","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). A default key tried after the configured one can log in as another account for the same reason the agent key did.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Verified with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"cargo run -p rc-git-cli -- fetch <repo>","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" on the failing repository, which returned ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"fetch origin up to date","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". A second alias repository still fetches, and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"scripts/check.sh --fast","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" passes.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Why This Works","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"GitHub decides the account during ssh user authentication and the repository permission only at ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"exec","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". It accepts the first offered key registered to any account, then checks whether that account can read ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"example-org/example-repo","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" when ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"git-upload-pack","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" runs. On a host like that, the key offer order is the account choice. OpenSSH's order is the contract that multi-account configs are written against: name the account's key with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentityFile","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", and optionally rule out the rest with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentitiesOnly","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". Matching agent keys to files by key data keeps the agent as the signer, so there is no passphrase prompt for a key the agent already holds, while the choice of key still comes from the config.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Rewriting ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentitiesOnly","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" as ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"User","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" reuses russh-config's own block matching and merge rule rather than adding a second host matcher that could drift from it. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"query","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" folds the matching blocks in file order (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"lib.rs:120-131","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"), and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"merge","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" fills a scalar field such as ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"user","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" only while it is still ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"None","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"lib.rs:52-72","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"identity_file","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" alone accumulates, ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"lib.rs:74-79","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). That is OpenSSH's first-value-wins rule, so ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IdentitiesOnly","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" resolves exactly as ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"User","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" would, including the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Host *","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" retry for globals above the first block.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
